      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While avoiding discrimination is legally and ethically paramount, it is true that managers must address unconscious biases and teach staff to separate genuine behavioral red flags from prejudiced assumptions. In high-end retail, \"vibes\" often stem from observable actions—such as groups lingering too long without touching items or individuals hesitantly moving toward locked glass cases—rather than appearance alone. Effective training focuses on converting these vague feelings into concrete, policy-driven observations that trigger a calm, professional response without violating store policies on disparate treatment.",
